WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.301
Welcome to our training on how to move your FTL shipments with Amazon Freight.

00:00:05.301 --> 00:00:05.680
Do

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.016
you have full truckload or FTL shipments to move?

00:00:09.016 --> 00:00:11.240
You can take advantage of Amazon's

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:16.320
advanced technology and network of over 30,000 Amazon-owned trailers and trusted

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.160
carriers to move your shipments inbound to Amazon, to your facilities and to

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:24.310
third-party facilities all with Amazon Freight.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.560
This training will cover benefits

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.373
of Amazon Freight and how to book and track your shipments.

00:00:30.373 --> 00:00:31.760
Amazon Freight offers a

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.560
variety of benefits to help ensure your shipment experience is simple and

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.810
reliable from start to finish.

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.960
Amazon Freight provides shippers with 24/7

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:47.200
network monitoring and customer support, GPS tracking and easy online payments.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.360
You'll have access to competitive and transparent spot rates or the option to

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.126
secure contract rates on your most used lanes.

00:00:55.126 --> 00:00:57.200
You can access your instant quote

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.291
directly on the Amazon Freight website.

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:02.080
All you need to provide is your shipment's

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.413
pickup city or zip code, delivery city or zip code and pickup date.

00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:07.080
To start

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.407
booking shipments with Amazon Freight, you'll first create a shipper account.

00:01:11.407 --> 00:01:11.800
Once

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.040
your account is created, you'll have immediate access to a spending limit so

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.880
you can start booking right away.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.640
Now let's cover how to book with Amazon Freight

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.966
starting with shipments inbound to Amazon.

00:01:22.966 --> 00:01:25.680
To book a fulfillment by Amazon or

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.800
FBA shipment inbound to Amazon, you'll first create an FBA shipment in Seller

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:31.218
Central.

00:01:31.218 --> 00:01:36.240
On step four of the send to Amazon workflow, confirm carrier and

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:41.340
pallet information and then select non-partnered carrier and other from the

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.526
carrier drop-down.

00:01:42.526 --> 00:01:46.480
Once your FBA shipment is created, visit the Amazon Freight

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:49.615
portal to book and schedule a pickup date for the load.

00:01:49.615 --> 00:01:51.040
To do this, visit the

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.406
shipments page and select new quote.

00:01:53.406 --> 00:01:56.560
On the get quote page, specify that your

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.000
shipment is going to an Amazon facility and provide both pickup and delivery

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.024
location information.

00:02:02.024 --> 00:02:06.120
In the delivery location field, provide the Amazon

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.391
facility code for your FBA shipment.

00:02:08.391 --> 00:02:11.040
Then select a requested pickup date for

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:11.825
your load.

00:02:11.825 --> 00:02:15.360
This date will be confirmed based on delivery appointment

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.672
availability once your booking is complete.

00:02:18.672 --> 00:02:20.880
Next, confirm your location

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.263
details.

00:02:21.263 --> 00:02:24.713
On the book shipment page, provide your shipment details.

00:02:24.713 --> 00:02:25.480
In the

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:30.040
purchase orders field, provide your Amazon reference ID from the FBA shipment

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.714
created in Seller Central.

00:02:31.714 --> 00:02:35.480
Once all your information is entered, you're ready to

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:36.495
book your shipment.

00:02:36.495 --> 00:02:39.880
You'll be directed to your confirmation page where you can

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.006
download your shipment's bill of lading or BOL.

00:02:43.006 --> 00:02:44.960
You'll also receive an email

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.620
confirming your shipment pickup date and time.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:49.520
For booking shipments outside of

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.200
Amazon, like to your facility or a third-party facility, visit the shipments page

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.811
and select new quote.

00:02:55.811 --> 00:02:59.840
On the get quote page, specify that your shipment isn't

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.520
going to an Amazon facility and provide pickup and delivery location details and

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:05.969
a pickup date.

00:03:05.969 --> 00:03:08.868
Once complete, click save and continue.

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:10.800
Next, confirm your location

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:11.297
details.

00:03:11.297 --> 00:03:15.767
On the book shipment page, input your shipment details.

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:16.760
Once all

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.862
information is entered, you can now book your shipment.

00:03:19.862 --> 00:03:21.240
You'll be directed to

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:25.373
your shipment's confirmation page where you can download your BOL.

00:03:25.373 --> 00:03:26.200
Once your

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.240
shipment is picked up, the view shipment details page will provide tracking

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:32.058
information for your shipment.

00:03:32.058 --> 00:03:35.240
Amazon owned trailers and trusted carriers are

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:39.960
equipped with GPS so you can have full visibility of your shipments from pickup

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:40.742
to delivery.

00:03:40.742 --> 00:03:45.040
For more information or to start booking, visit the Amazon Freight

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:45.398
website.

00:03:45.398 --> 00:03:49.700
This concludes our training on how to move your FTL shipments with

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:50.405
Amazon Freight.

00:03:50.405 --> 00:03:54.280
You now have the tools to move your shipments using Amazon's

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.055
network and technology.

00:03:56.055 --> 00:04:01.380
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store!
